From 13aa61fc7c73762d4216af8f1249e45b7ba62865 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:10:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] http/qt: One "Nintendo services" server for everything
 Nintendo

Replaces the separate SpotPass server and Nintendo services settings
(and the per-service switches) with one choice on Configure > General >
Network > Nintendo services: "Nintendo's servers" or "Custom server".

With a custom server, every http:C request (and every built-in SpotPass
download) meant for Nintendo goes to that address, keeping path and
query: any host under nintendo.net, nintendowifi.net or nintendo.com,
SpotPass addresses wrapped by Akamai and SpotPass on NetPass's mirror.
X-Tangelo-Original-Host names the Nintendo host, so one server or proxy
(nginx in Tangelo's server package) routes everything. Without a scheme
the address is http. The HLE game server login (frd) uses the same
server. The Nintendo Zone checkbox moves into this group.

Settings: use_custom_nintendo_server and nintendo_server_url replace
use_custom_spotpass_server, spotpass_server_url,
use_nintendo_services_server, nintendo_services_server_url and the
nintendo_services_conntest/nasc/nus switches (also on Android).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
